{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans","id":939652,"title":"Who exactly imprisoned the Titans?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-29T11:12:56-07:00","id":939652,"title":"Who exactly imprisoned the Titans?","content":"Did the gods do it? If so, which pantheons (bearing in mind that some pantheons, such as the Egyptians and the Norse, exist thousands of years apart from each other)? My personal theory is that the Titans are the Yozis of Exalted and were imprisoned thousands of years before recorded history. What is the canon answer to this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T13:46:53-07:00","id":939762,"title":"","content":"The canon answer from 1e is that there was a first Titanomachy, much like the one described in Theoi myths, wherein all of the gods of every pantheon, fought all of the Titans of every pantheon and imprisoned them. But honestly you can table rule whatever works best for your story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T14:23:25-07:00","id":939785,"title":"","content":"TheGraySoul is exactly right. Scion 1E simply rules it that all of the Pantheons fought a war and imprisoned the Titans. Despite the huge chronological issues in this, that is the reality that Scion 1E presents. The 1E canon answer is exceptionally Theoi-focused (most of 1E has a focus on the Greeks or Norse in the core systems of the game. It's a bit problematic.) such as even naming the Titans Titans.<br /> <br /> The way I get around this is use the idea of the Titanomachy like the Iron Age, in that it took place at a different time all over the globe, and in binding the Titans, both time and space got a bit confused and the world became what it is today. For example, the Tuatha fought a war with the Fomori some time before 500 BCE, while the Teotl would have founded The Fifth Sun later then that. It also explains why places like Hyperboria, Tir na nOg, and Olympus are not... there. Just how Time got fuddled by the removal of the Titans, places that were primarily legendary folded out of reality until the Titans are freed once again. It helps with the 'All Myths are True' problem as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T14:36:56-07:00","id":939794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=939785#post939785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TheGraySoul is exactly right. Scion 1E simply rules it that all of the Pantheons fought a war and imprisoned the Titans. Despite the huge chronological issues in this, that is the reality that Scion 1E presents. The 1E canon answer is exceptionally Theoi-focused (most of 1E has a focus on the Greeks or Norse in the core systems of the game. It's a bit problematic.) such as even naming the Titans Titans.<br /> <br /> The way I get around this is use the idea of the Titanomachy like the Iron Age, in that it took place at a different time all over the globe, and in binding the Titans, both time and space got a bit confused and the world became what it is today. For example, the Tuatha fought a war with the Fomori some time before 500 BCE, while the Teotl would have founded The Fifth Sun later then that. It also explains why places like Hyperboria, Tir na nOg, and Olympus are not... there. Just how Time got fuddled by the removal of the Titans, places that were primarily legendary folded out of reality until the Titans are freed once again. It helps with the 'All Myths are True' problem as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is some real nice explanation, Watcher, thank you very much. Reminds me of the Mage the Awakening philosophy regarding Atlantis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T14:56:11-07:00","id":939802,"title":"","content":"I hope the Titans are severely scaled back in 2e. They really don't fit with a decent number of the Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T15:15:05-07:00","id":939815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans#post939652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the gods do it? If so, which pantheons (bearing in mind that some pantheons, such as the Egyptians and the Norse, exist thousands of years apart from each other)? My personal theory is that the Titans are the Yozis of Exalted and were imprisoned thousands of years before recorded history. What is the canon answer to this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The best explanation is &quot;Schrodinger's Cat Theory&quot;<br /> <br /> The 1st edition book explains that all of the pantheon's creation myths are simultaneously true and false, which is why multiple gods can take credit for the same contributions to humanity. You've got Apollo driving his sun chariot across the sky, and at the same time, you have some Norse goddess being chased by wolves across the sky, and at the same time, Amaterasu is the one moving the sun, and so on.<br /> <br /> So in a way, all of the pantheons are responsible for sealing away the Titans. And I agree with your idea that this happened in the days before recorded history, which is why there are conflicting time periods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-29-2016, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T15:30:48-07:00","id":939827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=939794#post939794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is some real nice explanation, Watcher, thank you very much. Reminds me of the Mage the Awakening philosophy regarding Atlantis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! There are some problems with it, the Titan War stuff, and the Divine Geography, but thankfully the idea that imprisoning the Titans did something <i>odd</i> to the way Time and Space work really helps solve those with hand-waving.<br /> <br /> One of the more important things about it that I didn't mention if someone wants to use it is that 'Imprisonment' of the Titans isn't always literal. For example, Lir is a Titan in my games. He is imprisoned by his grief. Hadi, Skoll, Mani, and Sol are imprisoned by being stuck in an eternal chase with each other. Balor is imprisoned by being dead. Kagutsuchi is imprisoned by being butchered into several different Deities instead of one singular Titan. That helps solve the issue of 'Imprisonment in Tartarus' not making much sense for everyone who isn't Greek. (And even then, Atlas and Prometheus both were not imprisoned in Tartatus)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T22:56:10-07:00","id":939968,"title":"","content":"Hey, since clearly no astronauts have reported seeing a giant man holding the planet over his head, could that mean Atlas is stuck holding Terra over his head? Would Scions wishing to visit Atlas have to journey through Terra to reach him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T00:04:36-07:00","id":939981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=939968#post939968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, since clearly no astronauts have reported seeing a giant man holding the planet over his head, could that mean Atlas is stuck holding Terra over his head? Would Scions wishing to visit Atlas have to journey through Terra to reach him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! That's a really common misunderstanding of how Atlas works. Renaissance artists depicted Atlas holding the planet, but that's mostly because depicting his actual situation is sort of difficult, and somewhat less impressive. It's sort of caught on as the main 'image' of Atlas in cultural depictions modernly, but it doesn't make a lot of sense cosmologically for the Theoi. I'll give a quick rundown if anyone's interested!<br /> <br /> Atlas stands on Gaia, and holds Ouranos over his head. Sort of the easiest version of Greek Cosmology before the Philosophers got picking away at it and getting weird ideas is that reality is two bowls on top of each other forming a sphere. The upper bowl is Ouranos, and the lower Tartaros. This sphere of bowls is half filled with water, and Gaia rests at the center of this. Sort-of-floating, but there's also a connection running between herself and Tartaros evidenced by the fact Hades bridges the two. The water around the edge of the world (since it's essentially one colossal island) is Oceanos. Atlas stands on Gaia, somewhere by his daughters' garden, and holds Ouranos up above his head. I think somewhere around The Pillars of Heracles, by the Atlas Mountains is where he's noted to be? Can't remember for sure.<br /> <br /> Helpfully, they do also give us scale for this. If one dropped an anvil from the Heavens, it would take seven days falling to reach earth, and then another seven days to reach Tartaros.<br /> <br /> Edit: On the topic of space though, I just rule that just like the world, sealing the Titans also made that go a bit odd. Each Pantheon effectively has a different 'Outer Space', sort of like infinitely overlapped Terra Incognita, except they are all real, and our perception of Space's probably some sort of bad echo caused by all of these places existing on top of each other.<br /> <br /> For example, if a Theoi was sitting in the ISS, they would be floating in Chaos (the Primordial, they're not actually 'chaos' but more like 'the stuff outside Ouranos' IIRC. Nothing chaotic about them.) Helios, and Selene would be floating in the sky circling the bowls housing the earth. Ouranos is transparent, but from the bottom, Tartaros has been bound in... bronze? Yeah, bronze. Both the sun and moon are the same size as the other (to explain eclipses.) All the various figures made into stars would be 'out there'.<br /> <br /> If a Anunna Scion was sitting in the ISS, they would be floating way, way up really close to the first layer of Heaven. They would be able to see Sin, and Shamash, but would also have an exceptionally clear line of sight to the planets and stars around them. I'd probably give them a huge boost to Prophecy, and generally working out the will of the Pantheon.<br /> <br /> That is, of course, assuming the Titans had broken free. If they hadn't, it would just be the normal, mundane space. If multiple Scions or Legendary Beings were present in the ISS at the same time, highest Legend determines the dominant cosmology, or if a tie, roll Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":".  Edited to make my opening sound way less dickish. Real sorry, it's damn late over here. 07-30-2016, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T03:28:11-07:00","id":940030,"title":"","content":"2e's conception of titans definitely takes into account their odd fit with various pantheons. \u00c0w\u1ecdn \u00f2r\u00ec\u1e63\u00e0, for example, have nothing resembling titans in their source mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T09:15:08-07:00","id":940105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=939968#post939968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, since clearly no astronauts have reported seeing a giant man holding the planet over his head, could that mean Atlas is stuck holding Terra over his head? Would Scions wishing to visit Atlas have to journey through Terra to reach him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Space travel in the World is an interesting prospect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T09:42:08-07:00","id":940118,"title":"","content":"As Watcher states, there are really serious problems trying to pin down mythic events to history and pre-history as much as there are issues with trying to pin mythic or pre-modern cartography. You can't really even say something like &quot;The Titans were imprisoned in the Iron Age/ or at the Bronze to Iron Age transition&quot;. Not only is that a moving target depend on where and who you are talking about (to the point it might not even be a relevant concept at all), a lot of the myths seem to point to other and much more widely separated times. Comparative mythologists, even before you start taking it in the direction of the fantastic for a RPG, are all over the place. <br /> <br /> For example: Do Odin, et al. taking out Ymir represent the end of the Ice Age? (Which is intimated and posited in RAW.) That's a long, long, long time ago, if so. Does the war between the Aesir and the Vanir reflect the conflict between the ancestors of the Germanic and Norse peoples intruding into the territories of the previous cultures (which are more closely related to the later Celts in a very simplistic way of looking at the prehistory of Europe)? Maybe. It's as good a card toss into the hat as anything else. But, trying to do any of that pinning mythic events to chronological events seems to get counter-productive and really thorny (I mean, we're not even taking into account the whole development of these various characters through various iterations along various paths from an initial source...) Unless, of course, you want to use that idea for your game, e.g. the Vanir are part of the &quot;over-Pantheon&quot; of Celtic cultures that include the Tuatha De and the gods of the Welsh (and the Gaulish gods about which we have no myths). If that's something you want. then other pieces can fall into place... the aes sidhe and the alfar fit together, etc. But that's not the way it has to be (just because it's decent comparitive mythology) or even should be, if it doesn't suit your game where the &quot;mythic space&quot; of the Tuatha and that of the Aesir don't and or can't overlap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T12:34:12-07:00","id":940192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940030#post940030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e's conception of titans definitely takes into account their odd fit with various pantheons. \u00c0w\u1ecdn \u00f2r\u00ec\u1e63\u00e0, for example, have nothing resembling titans in their source mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>One odd thought to me is that the easiest fit for Titans in the Egypian Pantheon would be the Ogdoad, primordial deities of the unshaped abyss-ocean that cme before the world. And yet Geb is described as being a Titan despite not being adversarial whatsoever and belonging to the more current grouping of Netjer?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T12:53:30-07:00","id":940200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940192#post940192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One odd thought to me is that the easiest fit for Titans in the Egypian Pantheon would be the Ogdoad, primordial deities of the unshaped abyss-ocean that cme before the world. And yet Geb is described as being a Titan despite not being adversarial whatsoever and belonging to the more current grouping of Netjer?</div> </div> </div> </div>2e's moving away from a purely adversarial relationship between Gods and Titans. Some pantheons have managed to form alliances with some of the Titans, cf. the Theoi and Helios,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T13:14:51-07:00","id":940208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940200#post940200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e's moving away from a purely adversarial relationship between Gods and Titans. Some pantheons have managed to form alliances with some of the Titans, cf. the Theoi and Helios,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why distinguish them at all then? Why not just have them be older gods?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T13:46:33-07:00","id":940227,"title":"","content":"The distinction between Titan and God is more a political one than it is a metaphysical one.<br /> <br /> That said, there are notable metaphysical differences: the Titans understand the world through the perspective of the Purview they embody, reformatting the areas around them in line with their essence. Lacking any connection to humanity, any understanding of it, they have no real distinction between self and other - they don't really understand how dangerous their powers are to other people because they don't really have a <i>concept</i> of other people as a thing that exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T15:30:02-07:00","id":940300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940208#post940208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why distinguish them at all then? Why not just have them be older gods?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because that would be like walking up to a Titan and calling them a child. The Titans sired the Gods, they came first and should be addressed as such.<br /> <br /> Still, I like the idea of the Titans not being strictly enemies, as it opens some new possibilities for stories.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something else I'd like to imagine is that since Titans created Gods in the first place, they'd have the ability to create Scions, as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T15:53:33-07:00","id":940309,"title":"","content":"Reminds of a scion of Ryujin character idea I had who eventually won over Kamimusuhi and married her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T17:04:01-07:00","id":940346,"title":"","content":"(off topic) By the way, I would like to suggest that in 2nd edition, they include an enunciation guide for some of these pantheons. I pretty much ignore the Aztecs entirely because reading their language is like trying to speak Elder Scrolls Dwarven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-30-2016, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T01:00:32-07:00","id":940528,"title":"","content":"With Aztecs we just call them by their epithets. It's easier to call someone the Smoking Mirror than try to teach everyone in the group a proper pronunciation, especially since it often deters players who otherwise are interested.<br /> <br /> But as far as why Titans are different from just old gods; I think that defines 2nd edition's cosmology. Titans are less personalities or &quot;human&quot; they embody ideas and elements which does not make them evil, but always makes them dangerous to humans. What makes gods different from Titans is an embracing of humanity. It's why there are religions and not just fearful writings of powerful primal beings. They gain a lot by embracing humanity but lose a bit too. That is why it is political, but also an important metaphysical difference. Titans are different. In my mind it's like the difference between a lightning strike and the electricity running through wires. Same general properties? Yes, but one is more controlled and purposed and has a bit more finesse, while the other is wild, uncertain, but always primal. It's an important difference which doesn't require a good/evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T02:35:28-07:00","id":940546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940528#post940528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Aztecs we just call them by their epithets. It's easier to call someone the Smoking Mirror than try to teach everyone in the group a proper pronunciation, especially since it often deters players who otherwise are interested.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not just the people, it's anything having to deal with them. Such as their cultural equipment list, like the Maquahuitl.<br /> <br /> But yes, the Titans embody concepts of nature, while Gods embody concepts of humanity. A Titan of Lightning is just raw, electrical power. A God of Lightning takes that electrical power and turns it towards a purpose.<br /> <br /> The Greater Titans are unrelatable to the Gods (how does one relate to an active volcano, or a neutron star?) That's why they need Avatars, who give purpose and guidance to their power, savage though it may be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T08:45:17-07:00","id":940632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940346#post940346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(off topic) By the way, I would like to suggest that in 2nd edition, they include an enunciation guide for some of these pantheons. I pretty much ignore the Aztecs entirely because reading their language is like trying to speak Elder Scrolls Dwarven.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they've certainly followed common conventions to simplify some other pantheons to make them more pronounceable. Like not using Freyr, Baldr, Hodr, etc. Or the commonly known versions of the Greek names (which are close to, but not quite the same as they are typically written: Apollon - Apollo is the name of the deity declined). Or the Greek names for the Egyptian gods (Isis instead of Ese, Anubis instead of Anpu, etc.) And even when there is an &quot;accepted pronunciation&quot; it's going to be &quot;incorrect&quot;: Hera isn't &quot;HAYR uh&quot;, it's &quot;HEER uh&quot;. It's YOOP i tur not JOOP i tur (which is really just &quot;Zeus Pater&quot; taking into account the lack of a &quot;z&quot; sound in Latin). Japanese vowels are pretty complex, so you're almost certainly saying those names wrongs. Plus putting emphasis on all the wrong syllables. There are several sounds in Chinese that are assigned English letters that don't exactly match. X is more like &quot;s&quot;, but it's not REALLY &quot;s&quot;, it's a sound about half-way between &quot;s&quot; and &quot;sh&quot;. Gaelic pronunciation compared to the way words are written can seem insane (and to my mind, it is). And so on.<br /> <br /> So why not just try to come up with an &quot;English-Aztec-light&quot;? (Huitzilopochtli becomes something like &quot;Hutsilpokle&quot; pronounced &quot;HOOTs ihl pawk lee&quot;. It's not THAT far off...) Because there is a degree of cultural insensitivity there. There's that. Plus it's going to set people for failure, or at least at a disadvantage if they want to go outside Scion materials to learn more about the gods in question than their repackaged, collated Scion versions. (Which BTW is essential). But, to a degree the best reason (to me) is because a lot of the cooler pantheons that aren't so commonly known that their names have been Anglicized. If you're not going to use the Aztec gods because the names are agglutinations of consonants that don't typically occur in English, there are LOT of other pantheons that aren't going to come into play for pronunciation reasons (Pretty much ANYTHING in the Americas - Inca, Guarani, Mayan, Northwest Coast, Inuit... even Cherokee is very weird looking). There are a lot of examples elsewhere. If you don't like the Aztec names, the figures from the various Australian pantheons.... &lt;shudder&gt;. And then there's going for African pantheons from click languages. (Though, admittedly, there are definitely some that won't phase people too much... Polynesian phonology is euphonious to English speakers. Sumerian has a syllabic structure and familiar phoneme choices.) <br /> <br /> There is one bonus to these other, non-Anglicized names, they are typically set up where each letter represents a single sound (not of that &quot;s&quot; can be pronounced as either &quot;s&quot; e.g. &quot;cats&quot; or &quot;z&quot; , e.g. &quot;dogs&quot;), though not always (particularly with vowels and when there's been a language &quot;between&quot;, as in Nahuatl to Spanish to English). So, if there is a pronunciation guide, it's just going to be the fact that there are weird combinations most people aren't used to. Once you get used to saying &quot;tl&quot;, a lot of Nahuatl words aren't all that tough to say. <br /> <br /> But then, it's not that hard to say &quot;Baldr&quot; instead of Balder after a little practice either....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T10:25:41-07:00","id":940683,"title":"","content":"@Ajax FYI, 2e is going to be using the Egyptian names for the Netjer instead of the popular Greek ones. Praise Azar!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T14:19:59-07:00","id":940846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940546#post940546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, the Titans embody concepts of nature, while Gods embody concepts of humanity. A Titan of Lightning is just raw, electrical power. A God of Lightning takes that electrical power and turns it towards a purpose..</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a hard time with the idea that Titans embody concepts while Gods embody concepts of humanity. It feels that the Titans are simplistic, dumbed down and one dimensional. While this certainly could work for titans that in all the lore of a culture's myths get one or two lines of description about them like a name, who their immediate family is and 'violent god of storms and wars' it certainly doesn't play out for most of the Greek titans or any titan that is fleshed out a little bit. <br /> <br /> Helios has every bit as much personality that Apollo does, he mated with humans, had dealings with gods and heroes and was trusted by Zeus. Same with his sisters Selene and Eos. Sure later poets mostly supplanted them with Apollo and Artemis but they didn't distance themselves from humanity or want to destroy the gods after the war. Same goes with many of the other titans.<br /> <br /> I guess in my head the titans are the element or object incarnate but they are not regulated to some distant plane of existence of primordial incomprehensible energies and base thoughts, they are just thousands of years older than the gods and are perhaps a bit more jaded over that time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T14:41:21-07:00","id":940858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940846#post940846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a hard time with the idea that Titans embody concepts while Gods embody concepts of humanity. It feels that the Titans are simplistic, dumbed down and one dimensional. While this certainly could work for titans that in all the lore of a culture's myths get one or two lines of description about them like a name, who their immediate family is and 'violent god of storms and wars' it certainly doesn't play out for most of the Greek titans or any titan that is fleshed out a little bit.<br /> <br /> Helios has every bit as much personality that Apollo does, he mated with humans, had dealings with gods and heroes and was trusted by Zeus. Same with his sisters Selene and Eos. Sure later poets mostly supplanted them with Apollo and Artemis but they didn't distance themselves from humanity or want to destroy the gods after the war. Same goes with many of the other titans.<br /> <br /> I guess in my head the titans are the element or object incarnate but they are not regulated to some distant plane of existence of primordial incomprehensible energies and base thoughts, they are just thousands of years older than the gods and are perhaps a bit more jaded over that time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well what you're describing is how the Titans are portrayed in 1e. The Greater Titan shares its power between multiple bodies called Avatars. These avatars each embody a different aspect of the Greater Titan's collective power, but they have their own personalities and ambitions. Despite the fact they're part of the same collective entity, they're prone to just as much infighting as the Gods. You could. in theory, have a Titan who is simultaneously an enemy and a friend to the Gods because they have two different Avatars.<br /> <br /> The actual Greater Titans are the raw, primal concept. Akhetaten is the Greater Titan of Light, but without the avatar, Aten to guide its power, they wouldn't do much more than sit around looking pretty all day.<br /> <br /> <br /> Muspelheim is the Greater Titan of Fire, with Surtur embodying flame's destructive capabilities, while Prometheus embody's flame's power to create and inspire.<br /> <br /> Hope that explained it, couldn't think of a better way to phrase it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-31-2016, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T21:17:18-07:00","id":941021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940858#post940858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual Greater Titans are the raw, primal concept. Akhetaten is the Greater Titan of Light, but without the avatar, Aten to guide its power, they wouldn't do much more than sit around looking pretty all day.<br /> <br /> Muspelheim is the Greater Titan of Fire, with Surtur embodying flame's destructive capabilities, while Prometheus embody's flame's power to create and inspire.<br /> <br /> Hope that explained it, couldn't think of a better way to phrase it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying. I just disagree with the premise that an Avatar of something is smarter/better/more creative than the prime/primal being. An avatar of Odin would have limited levels of his abilities, it may be more magic/prophesy guy or more warrior/justice guy but it would never be able to out do him in any of his areas of interest and power. <br /> <br /> Maybe its just me but I look at an amalgamation of great beings of power more along the lines of what Onslaught was. You mix up Magneto, Professor X, Franklin Richards and Nate Grey.. and you get someone that has everything they both do (telepathy, telekinesis, energy projection, sensing mutant presences, manipulating magnetic fields, and affecting reality itself) wrapped up in a combination of their personalities, drives and goals that forms its own separate persona. Now the Primal being is terrifying and can actually start exert it's will to affect change or to exact vengeance on the pantheons that imprisoned it.<br /> <br /> I hope you understand I'm not disagreeing with you but the base idea itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T06:30:44-07:00","id":941154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940528#post940528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as far as why Titans are different from just old gods; I think that defines 2nd edition's cosmology. Titans are less personalities or &quot;human&quot; they embody ideas and elements which does not make them evil, but always makes them dangerous to humans. What makes gods different from Titans is an embracing of humanity. It's why there are religions and not just fearful writings of powerful primal beings. They gain a lot by embracing humanity but lose a bit too. That is why it is political, but also an important metaphysical difference. Titans are different. In my mind it's like the difference between a lightning strike and the electricity running through wires. Same general properties? Yes, but one is more controlled and purposed and has a bit more finesse, while the other is wild, uncertain, but always primal. It's an important difference which doesn't require a good/evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>You basically have it, yep. Titans are consumed by the metaphysical association with their Purview, Gods are not, even if they are both, say, Thunder or Dance. Gods have an intrinsic connection to humanity, and Titans don't.<br /> <br /> In 2e, you can relate to some Titans, even have relationships with them. Helios even had a Scion (Phaethon). But Prometheus didn't steal fire and gift it to humanity because he wanted to help people, he did it to watch the minds of thousands <i>burn</i>.<br /> <br /> A lot of the creator and primeval deities are classified as <i>Primordials</i>, entities of such grand stature and concept that they're difficult to interact with outside of an Overworld-aligned Terra Incognita. They take up the conceptual space of the Greater Titans, and often encompass world-bodies and conceptual underpinnings of the World. The Ogdoad are maybe the best example, but there's a lot of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-01T07:08:53-07:00","id":941169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=941021#post941021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get what you're saying. I just disagree with the premise that an Avatar of something is smarter/better/more creative than the prime/primal being. An avatar of Odin would have limited levels of his abilities, it may be more magic/prophesy guy or more warrior/justice guy but it would never be able to out do him in any of his areas of interest and power.<br /> <br /> Maybe its just me but I look at an amalgamation of great beings of power more along the lines of what Onslaught was. You mix up Magneto, Professor X, Franklin Richards and Nate Grey.. and you get someone that has everything they both do (telepathy, telekinesis, energy projection, sensing mutant presences, manipulating magnetic fields, and affecting reality itself) wrapped up in a combination of their personalities, drives and goals that forms its own separate persona. Now the Primal being is terrifying and can actually start exert it's will to affect change or to exact vengeance on the pantheons that imprisoned it.<br /> <br /> I hope you understand I'm not disagreeing with you but the base idea itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">I understand your point, too, and if I remember correctly, I think your idea has some basis in 1st edition. I think I remember reading that while the Avatars are sympathetically connected with the Greater Titans, they only have access to whatever powers and knowledge the Greater Titan chooses to share with them. So, in a way, you're right. The collective Titan does have more than the individual Avatar.<br /> <br /> But the reason why they need Avatars to begin with is because of the difference between Titans and Gods. As I understand it, the Gods symbolize mastery and control over the natural world, but the Greater Titans embody the natural world without supervision or control. They're not individual people, they are entire planes of existence populated by legions of servants they can produce on whim.<br /> <br /> Hephaestus and Loki are both Gods who are known for their power to control fire. But Muspelheim actually <i>is fire</i>, it's an entire realm dedicated to burning everything it comes into contact with both physical and metaphysical.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Drowned Road doesn't simply govern the crushing depths of the ocean, <i>it is the crushing depths of the ocean</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Terra doesn't merely govern the World, <i>it is the World</i> in a state untouched by human hands.<br /> <br /> <br /> That, I believe is why they need Avatars to serve as the instrument of their will. Because without a physical body, they are just pure, elemental forces. But there are different ways in which to interpret the nature of a Titan, which is why the Avatars can fight among each other, despite the fact they are sympathetically the same being.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T06:54:43-07:00","id":944282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/939652-who-exactly-imprisoned-the-titans?p=940528#post940528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as far as why Titans are different from just old gods; I think that defines 2nd edition's cosmology. Titans are less personalities or &quot;human&quot; they embody ideas and elements which does not make them evil, but always makes them dangerous to humans. What makes gods different from Titans is an embracing of humanity. It's why there are religions and not just fearful writings of powerful primal beings. They gain a lot by embracing humanity but lose a bit too. That is why it is political, but also an important metaphysical difference. Titans are different. In my mind it's like the difference between a lightning strike and the electricity running through wires. Same general properties? Yes, but one is more controlled and purposed and has a bit more finesse, while the other is wild, uncertain, but always primal. It's an important difference which doesn't require a good/evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Another way of looking at it might be a theatre. Pyrotechnics are not the same thing as a fire breaking out. A man playing the role of a bloody-handed murderer is not the same thing as having a serial killer leap onstage. A staged battle is not the same thing as a brawl in the stalls. One of the common roles of gods in real life is to translate the various untamed elements of the world into a form that humanity can engage with. Titans offer no such comfort, and don't really understand why they should. Rather than <i>people</i> who wield (and are wielded by) Purviews, they're more like <i>Purviews</i> which occasionally squeeze themselves into people-shaped suits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/605-revlid","name":"Revlid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar605_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}